[I] A specification that python filesystems should adhere to

[T] fsspec is a template or specification for a file-system interface, that
[T] specific implementations should follow, so that applications making use of
[T] them can rely on a common behaviour and not have to worry about the
[T] specific internal implementation decisions with any given backend.

[U] https://github.com/fsspec/filesystem_spec

